# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Burmy — .gitignore
#
# This file is deliberately the FIRST thing committed to this repository.
#
# Burmy handles personal financial data. The rules below are ordered so that the
# dangerous ones come first, and they are intentionally broad: it is far cheaper
# to force-add a file that was wrongly ignored than to scrub a real bank
# statement out of git history.
#
# Rule of thumb: if a file could contain a real transaction, a real balance, an
# account number, or a credential — it does not belong in this repository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── SECRETS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
# M10 production secrets are scoped by consumer (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md) —
# real .env.postgres / .env.database / .env.app / .env.tunnel / .env.backup
# on the VPS must never be committed; only their .example templates may be.
!.env.example
!.env.postgres.example
!.env.database.example
!.env.app.example
!.env.tunnel.example
!.env.backup.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.crt
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
cloudflared/
*.tunnel.json
.restic-password
secrets/

# ── REAL FINANCIAL DATA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Broad by design. Test fixtures are SYNTHETIC and live under tests/fixtures/,
# which is force-unignored at the bottom of this file.
*.csv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.ofx
*.qfx
*.qbo
*.pdf
/statements/
/exports/
/imports/
/archive/
/private/
**/real-data/

# ── DATABASE DUMPS & BACKUPS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.sql.bz2
*.backup
/backups/
/pgdata/
/restore/

# ── UPLOAD SCRATCH ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Statement uploads are written to a temp dir and deleted after parsing.
# If the cleanup ever fails, this guarantees the leftovers are not committed.
/tmp/
/uploads/
/var/

# ── NODE / PNPM ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.pnpm-debug.log*
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ── NEXT.JS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
next-env.d.ts
.vercel/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── TESTING ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
.nyc_output/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/playwright/.cache/
/blob-report/

# ── EDITORS & OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── LOGS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs may contain redaction bugs. Never commit them.
*.log
logs/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXCEPTIONS — synthetic test fixtures ONLY
#
# The blanket *.csv / *.xlsx rules above would otherwise swallow the test
# fixtures. These re-include ONLY files under tests/fixtures/.
#
# Every file matched here MUST be synthetic. Never place a real statement in
# tests/fixtures/ — the rules below would happily commit it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!tests/fixtures/**/*.csv
!tests/fixtures/**/*.xlsx
